# How to cite Culprit (Citation File Format 1.2.0). Validated in `just lint`
# and CI's lint job by a pinned cffconvert. No version or release date: none
# has been released yet.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or refer to Culprit, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: Culprit
abstract: >-
  A diagnostic engine for small teams. It compares what a system is meant to
  do (from its code and specifications), what an environment is configured to
  do, and what read-only probes observe, and treats the divergence between
  them as the finding. It walks the request path from a symptom with probes,
  recording an investigation whose every edge cites a reading, and judges
  whether a fix fixed it.
authors:
  - given-names: Joshua
    family-names: Heath
repository-code: "https://github.com/Josh-Heath123/Culprit"
license:
  - AGPL-3.0-only
  - Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - diagnostics
  - observability
  - incident response
  - configuration drift
  - static analysis
